WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.520
Messier

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.290
Hocchibi?

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.790
Hozuki...

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.170
I'm so glad you're okay...

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.540
What is this thing?

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.480
A creation of mine.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:52.480
Yours?

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.740
How?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.570
I found an old blueprint in the attic...

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.740
I modified the design and built it up,
little by little, over the last three years.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.700
Then...

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.670
You figured out the security code to the prototyping workshop?

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.750
When did that happen?

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.750
How did you not notice?

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:11.960
In just three years...

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.180
You did this by yourself?

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.260
Amazing...

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.010
Wait, what did you build this thing for, anyway?

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.680
I was hoping to use it to go to Japan.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:22.740
Why does it have missiles and stuff?

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.850
Because there are air pirates.

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.060
Or in case something else happens along the way...
These are just preventative measures.

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.690
I should charge you with excessive force used in self-defense.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.070
No way...

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:35.690
Just kidding!

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.890
I can't believe you made this.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.780
I'm so impressed, Hozuki!

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.080
You're definitely Galileo's descendant!

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.330
That thing is still creepy.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:02:04.600
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:01:53.380 --> 00:02:04.600
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.400
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:12.400
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:19.660
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:19.660
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.740
shinkuromanika

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.740
Synchromanica

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.280
itsu no ma ni ka

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.280
Before I know it

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.450
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.450
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:32.750
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:32.750
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:39.260
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:39.260
I can hear someone's dream

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:46.220
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:46.220
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.030
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:59.030
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.360
shinkuromanika

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:01.360
Synchromanica

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.490
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:05.490
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.540
shinkuromanika

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.540
Synchromanica

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.750
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.750
The synchrony of your life

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.670
You would be the laughingstock of the air pirates.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.340
Creepy.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:22.810
Why?

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:24.850
It isn't cute? It's a goldfish!

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:27.130
But <i>why</i> a goldfish?

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.730
You should've chosen something more intimidating, like a shark or a killer whale.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.350
But my goldfish...

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.740
It's about time.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.670
I'm so sorry.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.770
That little girl made this?

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:10.310
That's pretty impressive.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.310
Please stop gawking and just arrest them!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.330
They even had a large air-fish of their own...

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:18.820
It must be a pretty large organization.

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:21.730
They are most likely air pirates.

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.820
But it's rare for them to venture into a residential area...

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.330
They were asking about Galileo's inheritance.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.640
Oh?

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:31.830
And did that ring any bells?

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.570
Of course not!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.830
My parents never even mentioned there was such a thing.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.160
Ah, well...

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:43.320
Would you mind coming back to the station to give us the details?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.840
All of you, if possible.

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:54.080
Are you Hozuki Ferrari-chan?

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.410
I'm Anna Hendrix.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.190
Do you have a moment to talk?

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.660
Um, who are you?

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.420
Like I said, Anna Hendrix.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:06.720
I saved your sister, Hazuki-neesan.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.200
Saved?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.330
And this time, I'll save you.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.450
For that to happen, we have to leave right now, okay?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.000
Well, I expected you to say that...

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.720
All right, I'll show you why.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.210
Just don't scream.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:28.390
What is this about?

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.180
Just get in.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.930
We should do as he says.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:37.130
Having a gun pointed at me twice in one day...

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:40.270
It makes me wonder what fate has in store for me.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:44.890
Understand?

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:46.450
But why?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.450
There's one more: the youngest.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.100
Find her and bring her in.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.200
Yes, sir.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:04.590
Why? What for?

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:07.720
There's no guarantee that cops won't do bad things.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:13.470
Who <i>are</i> you, Anna-san?

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.410
There's definitely been a mistake.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.910
All this...

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.910
I mean, we didn't do anything wrong!

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.910
We'll rip them a new one later,
with compensation for damages.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:40.940
In any case, I'm calling my lawyer.

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.580
I hope Hozuki is okay.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.500
Sylvia Ferrari.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:45.670
Get out.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:48.050
Hey!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.930
Let us out too!

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.200
What's this about?

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.850
You're being released.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:56.100
Someone's here for you,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.210
so please direct your questions to them.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:09.630
Show me your face, Japanese.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.750
Sylvia has been released.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:25.670
But you won't set a single foot outside
this cell for the rest of your life.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.650
Nor will your daughters.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.380
We are very powerful...

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.890
Bear that in mind when you answer this question.

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.720
Where is Galileo's inheritance?

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:45.480
An autograph from a descendant of Galileo Galilei...

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.940
This is such a rare item!

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.650
Um...

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:52.920
Oh, I'm a Galileo geek.

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.090
A Galileo geek?

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.160
As a hobby, I started researching great historical figures.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.770
But I happened to notice a hidden code in Milton's <i>Paradise Lost</i>.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.420
When I decoded it,

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.780
I found an unpublished dialogue between him and Galileo!

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.340
Unpublished?

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.220
Yes!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.300
So I began to investigate all kinds of things about Galileo...

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:18.560
He observed the Moon with a homemade telescope

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:21.180
and left six sketches of what he saw.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.730
They're historically significant,
as they documented Earthshine for the world.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:27.020
You know about that, right?

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:36.730
Well, apparently a seventh sketch may exist...

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.870
But the intel on it isn't very credible.

00:08:39.350 --> 00:08:42.540
Anyway, it seems Galileo embedded clues in the six sketches

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.860
concerning a discovery that would even rival his defense of heliocentrism.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.810
And that discovery is Galileo's inheritance...

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:51.880
The Galileo Tesoro.

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:53.440
Tesoro?

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:56.130
You look unconvinced.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:09:01.140
At first, I was driven purely by curiosity,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:05.140
but eventually I found enough
information to fill an entire book.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:09.270
But shortly after my discovery,
strange men attacked me.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:12.280
Just like you and your family.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.110
And it wasn't just them, either.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:17.780
The air pirates are after me and the police are also involved.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.280
You saw what just happened, right?

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:22.990
Everyone is trying to find the Galileo Tesoro.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:26.540
I don't know exactly what it is, but...

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:32.050
Hello, Sylvia.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.550
Sir.

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:35.960
Were you harmed in any way?

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.090
To think that air pirates would get involved...

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:40.550
To be honest, that was unexpected.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:43.140
What is going on, sir?

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.430
Please explain.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.040
What will happen to my daughters?!

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.040
Calm down...

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:53.240
You are one of our employees,
and an excellent one at that.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:58.280
I always keep an eye on you and make sure you're well-treated.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.240
That goes for tonight, too.

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:01.450
Sir?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.830
Right now, I hear a certain phrase
is making the rounds in the city.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.460
"Where is Galileo's inheritance?"

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.840
Maybe I should also jump on the bandwagon.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.000
Sylvia, where is Galileo's inheritance?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:20.340
You can ask all you want,

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:23.250
but Sylvia's his actual descendant.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.610
I really have no idea.

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:29.140
I don't even know what this inheritance is.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.980
I'd assumed as much.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:35.040
But are you sure you never heard anything?
Not even during pillow talk?

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.030
Unfortunately, for the past few years, we've slept in separate beds!

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.780
And what's the story behind that goldfish mecha?

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:45.490
I found an old blueprint in the attic...

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:48.860
That mecha is just something Hozuki put together in her spare time!

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.500
It has nothing to do with Galileo!

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:52.410
I see.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.750
Then let's see what your three sweet daughters have to say.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.920
I'll try to ensure they don't faint from pain.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:00.000
Wait!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.530
Don't you dare lay a finger on my girls!

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.730
If you remember anything,

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:06.010
notify one of the policemen here.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:09.640
You... You're not a cop?

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:18.070
Kakkii, do you have any candy on you?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.940
I can't believe you.

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.200
How can you be hungry at a time like this?

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.890
Crisis or not, a girl has to eat.

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:28.250
You can still feel hungry after getting dumped, or even after somebody dies.

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:29.830
So, candy?

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:31.120
Nope.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.450
Man, you're so useless!

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:38.530
I wonder what's going on with Hocchii...

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:45.680
What, and where, is the Galileo Tesoro?

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:50.520
To solve the mystery, I'll need help from all of you.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.350
We can't let it fall into their hands at any cost.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:58.560
I'm drawn to Galileo because his discoveries and inventions

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:01.080
were for humanity's benefit as a whole.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:06.490
The Galileo Tesoro shouldn't be
monopolized or kept secret, either.

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.490
Don't you agree, Hozuki-chan?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.850
Okay.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:16.730
I guess I can't blame you.

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:20.760
Let's revisit this conversation after we save everyone, okay?

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:23.940
Save everyone?

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:25.650
Of course.

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:26.760
Me?

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.560
Who else?

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:31.450
N-No... No way!

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.390
What do you mean?

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:35.280
I can't do anything!

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:37.520
We should let the police handle it...

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:41.700
Hozuki-chan, if you don't go help your family,

00:12:41.700 --> 00:12:44.030
you have no idea what could happen to them.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.140
Actually, that's a lie.

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.020
It's easy to imagine what would happen.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:49.910
They'd be killed!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.670
No...

00:12:53.220 --> 00:12:56.500
You're the only one who can save them, Hozuki-chan!

00:12:58.390 --> 00:12:59.930
The only one...

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.760
Can I really do it?

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.010
You can.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.760
Why?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.640
Because I'm a descendant of Galileo?

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.140
No, because they're your family.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:19.150
My family is in pieces.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.030
But...

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:29.120
If we could be close again, like we used to be...

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.410
If things could go back to how they were...

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:38.690
Need!

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:51.720
There she is!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:58.060
Hozuki Ferrari-san?

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.210
You aren't...

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:02.730
Who are you?

00:14:03.140 --> 00:14:04.310
Pardon.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:12.680
Put your hands behind your head and slowly turn around.

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.440
That gun's way too small!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.950
Damn it.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:43.980
Please...

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.990
Roger!

00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:56.710
You know, Hocchii...

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:01.040
She used to get lost pretty often.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.340
She wasn't lost.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:10.050
She'd spend hours staring at someone's mini-fish.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.300
Then<i> I'd</i> be the one sent out to find her.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:15.960
That one time we lost sight of her,

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:19.960
we found her dismantling Sylvie's mini-fish, right?

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:24.690
I wonder if she's okay...

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:28.490
She must have left the country by now.

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.320
She's smarter than she looks.

00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:36.930
Bring Hazuki and Kazuki to the interview room.

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.090
You don't really mean to shoot them, do you?

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:43.540
As long as they reveal its location,
there will be no need for bloodshed.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.650
We can't have you using firearms in the station.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.550
Besides, they're still children!

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:53.060
Death knows neither time nor place.

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:56.050
It is fair and merciful to none, Cassini.

00:15:56.580 --> 00:15:58.300
But, sir...

00:15:58.300 --> 00:16:03.060
Your job is to find Hozuki and bring her in.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:06.730
We're looking, but we haven't the faintest idea...

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.420
What the hell is that?!

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.270
What?

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.620
Ow...

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.050
Did that do the job?

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.100
The holding cells are underground.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.050
Can you move?

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:38.560
I'll try.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:42.890
Shoot it!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.650
Something's happening upstairs!

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:54.860
Bring your guns!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.530
Requesting backup!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.200
Bring Kevlar and riot shields!

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.700
What's going on?

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.210
I have to...

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.160
I have to do this!

00:17:09.060 --> 00:17:10.550
Stop right there, bastard!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.330
What're you guys doing?

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:22.060
Stop that thing!

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.210
What's with all that noise?

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.900
Is it those air pirates again?

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.020
What's wrong?

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:34.610
It's really hot in here.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:38.110
The suit's thermostat is broken...

00:17:38.470 --> 00:17:39.770
The temperature is going to keep rising,

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:40.870
so try to hurry!

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:42.740
Okay.

00:18:03.570 --> 00:18:04.220
Hocchii?

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:06.230
Hocchii?!

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:08.980
Haa-nee! Kaa-nee!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.110
Just a second...

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:14.900
Hocchii, don't push it!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:23.100
I'm sorry I took so long.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:23.870
Where's Mama?

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:25.620
They took her.

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.330
Stay behind me!

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.760
Papa!

00:18:49.760 --> 00:18:51.680
Hozuki? Hozuki, is that you?

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:53.170
What is this thing?

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.320
I made it.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.150
Let's get out of here first!
We're in huge trouble!

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:59.450
Hozuki, get to the roof ASAP.

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.410
I'll be waiting there with the <i>Galileo</i>.

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.130
The <i>Galileo</i>?

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:04.480
Your mecha.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.310
I figured "Goldfish" sounded kind lame, don't you think?

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.180
Cease fire!

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.180
I've never seen that suit before.

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:33.690
Did you make it yourself?

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:39.170
Very impressive, Hozuki Ferrari.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:41.530
Did you get those skills from your father?

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:45.700
Unfortunately, she got them from her mother.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:54.070
Stop right there.

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:56.630
Out of the way!

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.800
If the enemy's after Galileo's secrets,

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:10.960
you three should be the ones to discover them.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.970
Break Galileo's hold on our family.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:14.770
But what about you, Dad?

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.730
I've always been the muscle of the family.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.930
Your Mama may trump me in brains...

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:20.740
But you know what?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.950
When it comes to backbone, I beat her any day!

00:20:35.190 --> 00:20:37.400
Do you think Papa will be okay?

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:39.370
We have to believe in him.

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:50.970
Here.

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.780
Take it, quick.

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:54.980
Unless you want Hazu-nee to take it.

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:56.480
Are you all okay?

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:58.820
Who are you?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.880
Huh? You don't know each other?

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:13.120
Papa, we have a small problem.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.130
Same here.

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:18.750
Come back as quickly as you can, Roberto.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
